beta1.mono.official [d33da79d3]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta1.mono - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6614) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e50686f4-088b-4fe1-9e96-f4b7f82c6126)\n\nTo speed up playtesting iterations, I created a feature to test scenes with their own arbitrary execution argument options, and at the time, I made it clear to distinguish them from the Godot engine's execution arguments by putting in parameters with just `--`.\nAfter updating the project to `4.4-beta.1`, I realized that the Game Editor was not embedding only when I started playtesting with the features I had created and started investigating the issue.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7ad4808-97bc-4a24-851c-630e61e24677)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c040191-3ad5-43d0-a96f-9c8c7e8954b4)\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d33da79d3f8fe84be2521d25b9ba8e440cf25a88/editor/plugins/game_view_plugin.cpp#L566-L603\n\nI noticed that the parameters that seem to be needed for handling window embedding in the Game editor added in 4.4 go after `main_run_args`.\nI suspect this was caused by the function not working properly because it was blocked by the `--` that separates Godot arguments.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create or open any project.\n- Open project settings and turn on advanced settings then find `main_run_args`. (`editor/run/main_run_args`)\n- Put `--` in `main_run_args` and start play test.\n- You can see game window are separated from game editor window.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[game-editor-window-not-embedded-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18455857/game-editor-window-not-embedded-mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"ht